      "name": "Range Rover 2.0 Engine Specialists — FAQs",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.0#webpage"
      },
      "inLanguage": "en-GB",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.0#faq-question-1",
          "name": "Which Range Rover models use a 2.0 litre engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The 2.0 litre Ingenium engine is used across the Range Rover Evoque and Range Rover Velar, in petrol, diesel and plug-in hybrid (P400e) form. Power outputs vary by engine code, with P200, P300 and D200 among the most common variants fitted to these models."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.0#faq-question-2",
          "name": "Is the Range Rover 2.0 Ingenium engine reliable?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Overall, Ingenium engines are reasonably dependable when serviced correctly, but early diesel units built between 2015 and 2018 are well known for premature timing chain wear. Later revisions addressed this, so reliability depends heavily on build date, service history and how promptly early symptoms were investigated."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.0#faq-question-3",
          "name": "What are the common problems with the 2.0 diesel Ingenium engine?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Timing chain wear is the most widely reported issue on early builds, often signalled by a rattling noise on start-up or fault codes linked to cam timing. Other reported concerns include turbo wear and oil consumption, both of which are worth checking during a proper inspection."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.0#faq-question-4",
          "name": "How much does a Range Rover 2.0 engine replacement cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Cost depends on the engine variant, the extent of damage, and whether a repair, reconditioned unit or full replacement is the right fix. We assess each vehicle individually and provide a clear, itemised quote once diagnosis is complete, rather than a generic figure."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.0#faq-question-5",
          "name": "How do I know if I need a repair or a full replacement?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "This comes down to proper diagnosis. Some issues, like an early-stage timing chain rattle, can be resolved with a targeted repair, while significant internal damage usually points to a rebuild or replacement. We'll always explain the reasoning behind our recommendation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.0#faq-question-6",
          "name": "Do reconditioned Range Rover 2.0 engines come with a warranty?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, reconditioned and replacement engines are supplied with warranty cover. We'll confirm the exact terms for your specific engine and vehicle before any work is booked, so there are no surprises afterwards."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.0#faq-question-7",
          "name": "Do you collect the vehicle or do I need to bring it in?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We can discuss collection options alongside drop-off at our Grays workshop, depending on your location and the nature of the work. Get in touch and we'll confirm the most convenient arrangement for your vehicle."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://rangerovergarage.co.uk/engines/range-rover-2.0#faq-question-8",
          "name": "What areas do you cover for Range Rover engine work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We're based in Grays, Essex, and regularly support customers across Essex, London and the wider South East, alongside UK-wide enquiries for engine supply and fitting. Contact us to confirm availability for your location."
          }
        }
      ]
